This repo stores the code and infrastructure to analyze airline flight delays in an automated way. 
The goal was to be able to take in data from the airline data, provided by the government, shown [here][https://www.transtats.bts.gov/DL_SelectFields.aspx?gnoyr_VQ=FGJ&QO_fu146_anzr=b0-gvzr] and see what insights the data can provide.

I wanted to use this data set to showcase handling of real world data (i.e. Not Astronomy data), use of SQL using sqlite in Python, as well as data anlytics techniques. 
I wanted to also automate ingestion so that this process is scalable with the addition of new data with the following goals:
- to run on the fly 
- append to the database and 
- recompute tables and quanitites of interest in ones go.
Due to the on-the-fly nature of this code, it can output tables ready to be used in your favorite vizualization tool of choice such as Tableau, Power BI, etc. 

I have made some Tableau worksheets and can be found here.
